     The pprrooccssttaatt__ggeettggrroouuppss() function gets a pointer to the _p_r_o_c_s_t_a_t struc‐
     ture, a pointer to _k_i_n_f_o___p_r_o_c structure, and returns the process groups
     as a dynamically allocated array of _g_i_d___t elements.  The caller is re‐
     sponsible to free the allocated memory with a subsequent
     pprrooccssttaatt__ffrreeeeggrroouuppss() function call.

     The pprrooccssttaatt__ggeettkkssttaacckk() function gets a pointer to the _p_r_o_c_s_t_a_t struc‐
     ture initialized with one of the pprrooccssttaatt__ooppeenn__**() functions, a pointer
     to _k_i_n_f_o___p_r_o_c structure, and returns kernel stacks of the process as a
     dynamically allocated array of _k_i_n_f_o___k_s_t_a_c_k structures.  The caller is
